## Test Anti-Pattern Audit: `ProductCatalogTests.cs`

### Summary

| Severity | Count |
|----------|-------|
| **Critical** | **6** |
| Medium | 2 |
| Low | 1 |

This is a textbook **coverage-touching** test suite. Every public method is invoked (achieving that 95% metric), but almost nothing is actually verified. These tests will pass even if the production code is completely broken — which explains the production bugs.

---

### 🔴 Critical Findings

#### 1. Coverage-Touching (Systemic) — entire class

The test class methodically calls every public member in declaration order with no meaningful assertions. 6 of 10 tests have **zero assertions**; the remaining 4 use only `Assert.IsNotNull` — the weakest possible check.

---

#### 2. No Assertions — `AddProduct_Works` (line 17)

```csharp
// BEFORE — proves nothing
_catalog.AddProduct(product);

// FIX — verify product was persisted
_catalog.AddProduct(product);
var retrieved = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.AreEqual("Widget", retrieved!.Name);
Assert.AreEqual(9.99m, retrieved.Price);
```

#### 3. No Assertions — `UpdatePrice_Works` (line 32)

```csharp
// FIX — verify price actually changed
_catalog.UpdatePrice("SKU-001", 14.99m);
var updated = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.AreEqual(14.99m, updated!.Price);
```

#### 4. No Assertions — `RemoveProduct_Works` (line 38)

```csharp
// FIX — verify product is gone
_catalog.RemoveProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.IsNull(_catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001"));
```

#### 5. No Assertions — `GetProductCount_Works` (line 63)

```csharp
// FIX — verify count
var count = _catalog.GetProductCount();
Assert.AreEqual(0, count);
```

#### 6. No Assertions — `ApplyBulkDiscount_Works` (line 68)

This is the most dangerous — a 10% discount calculation is never verified. A bug in the math (`Price * fraction` instead of `Price * (1 - fraction)`) would never be caught.

```csharp
// FIX — verify discounted prices
_catalog.ApplyBulkDiscount(0.10m);
Assert.AreEqual(8.991m, _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001")!.Price);
Assert.AreEqual(17.991m, _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-002")!.Price);
```

#### 7. No Assertions — `ImportFromCsv_Works` (line 85)

```csharp
// FIX — verify imported data
_catalog.ImportFromCsv("SKU-001,Widget,9.99");
var imported = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.IsNotNull(imported);
Assert.AreEqual("Widget", imported.Name);
Assert.AreEqual(9.99m, imported.Price);
```

